From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: mixer: Run the H616 display engine at 696 MHz

Allwinner's own tree runs the H616's display engine at 696 MHz (pll-de
and de, assigned-clock-rates 696000000), and stock firmware reads it
back at that rate. Mainline set 600 MHz, which cuts the VI scaler's
throughput by the same proportion. Use the vendor's rate; the DE PLL
makes it as 24 MHz x 29.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
@@ -1171,7 +1171,8 @@
 
 static const struct sun8i_mixer_cfg sun50i_h616_mixer0_cfg = {
 	.de_type	= SUN8I_MIXER_DE33,
-	.mod_rate	= 600000000,
+	/* Allwinner's own rate, the scaler's headroom */
+	.mod_rate	= 696000000,
 	.has_formatter	= 1,
 };
 
